feat(fwlog): read the firmware KFLG ring from a dedicated driver

The firmware keeps a 256 KiB ring at the fixed physical address 0xF44C0000:
KebabFwLogDxe reserves the region as EfiReservedMemoryType, writes the 'KFLG'
header and the framebuffer serial library appends every byte it renders.  The
kernel could already see the page but the only reader was a function appended
to kebab_spmi.c by a local script, with a fixed 6144-byte limit and no boot
line.

Move the reader into bsd/dev/kebab_fwlog.c and list it in bsd/conf/files, so
kebab_spmi.c stays the PMIC/RPMh driver.  kebab_fwlog_attach() maps the 256 KiB
exactly once, validates magic 0x474c464b and a data size in 1..0x40000-16, and
caches the mapping; the io_map submap is only 8 MiB, so a second map is never
attempted, not even after an invalid header.  A missing or implausible header
is reported once with the address and the value that was read.

kebab_fwlog_report(max_bytes) prints the newest max_bytes oldest-first.  It
advances the start to just past the first newline, but scans only the first
half of the window so a buffer without a newline still prints; it drops CR and
batches the console into 192-byte writes.  max_bytes == 0 means the whole ring,
but the USB console ring is 16 KiB (16383 usable) and a larger burst drops
bytes, so that case is capped at 12288 bytes and the header says it was capped.
The header prints ring and written; a closing line prints how many bytes were
actually emitted.

kebab_fwlog_boot_summary() prints one line - ring bytes and total written -
right after the USB console is started in bsd_init.

The console command follows SPMI?/PON?: "FWLOG?\n" dumps 4096 bytes, and
"FWLOG? all\n" asks for the whole ring.  Both are matched in the existing
bulk-OUT completion window and in the KDP-anchored path, so a command still
has to arrive in one transfer.

Verified: applies to 1b191cb as the last patch of the series (after 0128,
which touches only bsd/dev/kebab_spmi.c and does not collide with these
files); the kernel builds on the macOS 14.6 build VM and the new strings and
symbols are present in kernel.development.kebab.  Not yet run on the device.

